          "**Featured Stories**",
          "• DeepSeek drops an “intermediate” model — and slashes API costs Sept 29, 2025 — Reuters Chinese AI firm DeepSeek launched V3.2-Exp, a transitional model featuring its new Sparse Attention system for faster, cheaper long-text processing. Alongside the release, the company cut API prices by over 50%, undercutting global rivals. ([reuters.com](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Freuters%2Ecom&urlhash=QXZY&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)) Why it matters: this isn’t just another model drop — it’s a strategic move to compete on efficiency and affordability, reshaping market dynamics in China and beyond.",
          "• Senators propose mandatory AI risk evaluations Sept 29, 2025 — Axios Senators Hawley and Blumenthal introduced the Artificial Intelligence Risk Evaluation Act, requiring advanced AI models to undergo DOE-run risk reviews before launch. ([axios.com](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Faxios%2Ecom&urlhash=3y-e&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)) This could be the U.S.’s first step toward pre-deployment safety checks — shifting the burden from “fix it later” to “prove it’s safe first.”",
          "• Google Search goes conversational with “Search Live” Sept 24, 2025 — The Verge Google rolled out Search Live, merging voice queries and real-time camera inputs into conversational, agent-like search interactions. ([theverge.com](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Ftheverge%2Ecom&urlhash=v54j&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)) The future of search isn’t keywords — it’s dialogue. And this is Google’s clearest pivot yet toward an agentic interface.",
          "• Humain Horizon Pro: an AI-native laptop with its own OS Sept 2025 — Tom’s Guide Qualcomm and Humain unveiled the Horizon Pro, running Humain One OS and optimized for local model workloads like ALLAM. ([tomsguide.com](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Ftomsguide%2Ecom&urlhash=h5oY&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)) This isn’t just a spec bump — it’s the dawn of agent-first devices.",
