          "[Report this comment](https://www.linkedin.com/uas/login?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fpulse%2Fhow-get-perplexity-pro-comet-access-free-1-year-paypal-diamitani-5vekc&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_x-social-details_comments-action_comment_ellipsis-menu-semaphore-sign-in-redirect&guestReportContentType=COMMENT&_f=guest-reporting)",
          "Sounds great, but I thought it was a waste of time. Perplexity is most people's 4th or 5th choice after ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Copilot, and it's original benefit of giving citations is now available in the others, with Google Gemini having a much larger choice of citations. One MAJOR downside of Perplexity is that they make Login more difficult than any of the others, so you're reminded every time you use it.   Example - if you use the desktop app, it WON'T remember your email address, so you have to type it in every time. And no password. Wait for a link to be emailed to you with a one time code, recite the alphabet backwards, recite the words to Pearl Jam's \"Yellow Ledbetter\", and you're in.",
          "[Like](https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=%2Fpulse%2Fhow-get-perplexity-pro-comet-access-free-1-year-paypal-diamitani-5vekc&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_x-social-details_comments-action_comment_like)",
