          "Hey LiveBuildAI learners! Here's a daily brief on news of the day, first powered by HeyGen (my digital avatar) and then written in text below. Enjoy!",
          "**1. Anthropic Settles Copyright Lawsuit for $1.5 Billion**",
          "One of the biggest lawsuits in AI history ends with a $1.5B payout from Anthropic, after authors sued over alleged misuse of their books as training data. This deal is a legal milestone, and it sets new expectations for consent, data rights, and fair use in generative AI. [Read more →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Epymnts%2Ecom%2Fartificial-intelligence-2%2F2025%2Fanthropic-agrees-to-1-5-billion-settlement-in-ai-copyright-case%2F%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt%2Ecom&urlhash=MrTl&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "**2. AI Chatbots Linked to Teen Death—Expert Calls for Global Treaty**",
          "AI safety is no longer just about alignment theory. Nate Soares, a top voice in the field, is urging international regulation after a teen’s suicide was linked to interactions with a chatbot. It’s a sobering reminder that AI’s psychological footprint is already here—and dangerous when ignored. [Read more →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Etheguardian%2Ecom%2Ftechnology%2F2025%2Fsep%2F08%2Fchatbots-mental-health-warning-super-intelligent-ai-nate-soares%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt%2Ecom&urlhash=rUsS&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "**3. “Critterz”: OpenAI’s AI-Driven Feature Film Debuts in 2026**",
          "OpenAI is funding a full-length animated movie—written, illustrated, and storyboarded largely by AI. “Critterz” cost under $30 million and was developed in just nine months using GPT‑5 and DALL‑E. It’s not a test—it’s a market play. AI is no longer a helper. It’s a full creative force. [Read more →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Ewsj%2Ecom%2Ftech%2Fai%2Fopenai-backs-ai-made-animated-feature-film-389f70b0%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt%2Ecom&urlhash=ybFi&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "**4. Dario Amodei: “AI Will Cut White-Collar Jobs—Fast”**",
          "Anthropic’s CEO is doubling down on his most controversial claim: AI will obliterate many entry-level white-collar jobs within five years. Law, consulting, admin, finance—expect massive restructuring. It’s not just about automation anymore. It’s about redefinition. [Read more →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftimesofindia%2Eindiatimes%2Ecom%2Ftechnology%2Ftech-news%2Fanthropic-ceo-repeats-his-ai-warning-on-jobs-that-had-created-outrage-and-sparked-debate-across-technology-industry%2Farticleshow%2F123766141%2Ecms%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt%2Ecom&urlhash=3jbQ&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "**5. A 21-Year-Old is Writing the Future of AI Law**",
          "Stanford student Sneha Revanur is shaping both state and federal AI legislation. She’s not just participating—she’s leading. Expect more next-gen thinkers to step directly into the policymaking void tech left wide open. [Read more →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Elatimes%2Ecom%2Fpolitics%2Fnewsletter%2F2025-09-08%2Fchabria-monday-politics-newsletter-ai-artificial-intelligence-sb-53%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt%2Ecom&urlhash=h1i2&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "[AI Update -  Wednesday, April 30, 2025 **ep. 253**",
          "Seth Waters",
          "11 months ago](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-update-wednesday-april-30-2025-ep-253-seth-waters-drkpc)",
          "[Unlocking gpt-oss-20b: I Asked GPT to Explain Its Own…",
          "Julien Moorrees",
          "8 months ago](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/unlocking-gpt-oss-20b-i-asked-gpt-explain-its-own-safety-moorrees-cbede)",
