          "Florent Daudens",
          "1 year ago](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-news-we-losing-our-voice-florent-daudens-5tsoe)",
          "**New Tools to Watch**",
          "Pushing into new territory—one category at a time.",
          "**Video AI – Pika Labs**",
          "Create dynamic, cinematic video from a single text prompt. The latest models handle motion and scene coherence far better than earlier tools. Great for product promos, animation ideation, or short-form storytelling. Try Pika →",
          "**Creativity – RunwayML Gen-3 Alpha**",
          "This is the bleeding edge of generative video. Runway’s Gen‑3 model handles lighting, pacing, and cinematic transitions with serious flair. It’s currently invite-only, but it’s setting the benchmark for what AI-assisted filmmaking looks like. Explore Runway →",
          "**Research & Docs – Perplexity Pages**",
          "Go beyond chat. Perplexity now lets you turn conversations into beautiful, cited research pages—instantly. Think Notion meets AI-powered curation. Perfect for thought leadership, internal wikis, or deep dives. [Try it →](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Eperplexity%2Eai%2F&urlhash=rSLf&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)",
          "**General Consumer – HeyGen**",
          "Create lifelike avatars for presentations, customer support, or content delivery. Combine script input with AI actors in multiple languages. Surprisingly realistic—and scalable for solopreneurs and teams alike. Explore HeyGen →",
          "**What This All Signals**",
          "• The legal firewall around AI just got real. Consent and IP usage will reshape how we build.",
          "• Chatbots aren’t toys. If they’re causing harm, it’s time to reconsider default deployments.",
          "• AI creativity is moving fast—and skipping straight to finished products.",
          "• Job losses aren’t future-tense—they’re forecasted. It’s time to re-skill, not just observe.",
          "• Policy isn't a spectator sport anymore. It's peer-driven, and next-gen voices are in the room.",
          "Back tomorrow with more breakthroughs, frictions, and signals that matter. —Patrick",
